From b2753077aca87082d31f3470d2d02e9a7318815c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:01:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] A steer never kills a running tool: Claude moves it to the
 background, as its own terminal does

The person's steer during a running command used to stop the turn first
(an `interrupt`): Claude Code killed the Bash and told the model the person
didn't want to proceed, so agents halted or thought they were refused.

Claude Code from 2.1.286 takes the person's message as its terminal does:
`priority: "now"` with `origin: {kind: "human"}` moves a running shell
command, subagent or MCP call (and from 2.1.287 WebFetch/WebSearch) to the
background, uninterrupted, and the model reads the message in the same turn.
On such a CLI (read through the cached version probe) the person's steer
goes that way and the engine stops nothing first: `steer_stops_tool` is
version-gated and read off the async threads at dispatch. An older or
unknown CLI keeps the old path. A message from another chat never claims a
human origin: `next` while a tool runs, as before. Stop stays a hard stop.

What the CLI sends then, captured live on 2.1.328 (fixtures
live-2.1.328-steer-{bash,agent,mcp,webfetch}.jsonl):
- Bash: a result naming its task (`backgroundTaskId`,
  `backgroundedToDeliverMessage`), `task_updated {is_backgrounded}`, the
  roster entry, a `task_notification` at its end and a wake turn. It now
  reads as a background command (no exit code, its note as output) rather
  than one that exited 0.
- A subagent: the usual background launch ("Async agent launched"); its
  chip runs on until its notification, as a background agent's does.
- MCP: an `mcp_task` in the roster, a "moved to the background" result, a
  notification and a wake turn. It is listed with the background shells
  and waited on, as a background agent is.
- WebFetch: `{detachedToolCall: true}` and one result only; its answer
  comes in the wake turn. Every turn still ends on its own result.

ACP: a steer into a turn the agent continued on its own (a background
wake) sent `session/cancel` because a tool was open, killing it. It now
waits for the open tools and cancels once the last one closes. Tool calls
in the injection drain are tracked too. Codex, Muse, Cursor, OpenCode and
Pi already wait for or inject past running tools; ACP's step-boundary
preempt already waited.
