+/// The first CLI that takes the person's steer the way its own terminal
+/// does: a `now` line marked `origin: {kind: "human"}` moves a running shell
+/// command, subagent or MCP call to the background and the model reads the
+/// message in the same turn; nothing is interrupted unless the work can't
+/// move (WebFetch and WebSearch move from 2.1.287). Live-verified on 2.1.328:
+/// the call's result says it was moved (`backgroundTaskId` on a Bash
+/// result, `detachedToolCall` on a fetch), its task reports through the
+/// usual `task_notification` and wakes the session when it ends.
+const STEER_MOVES_TOOLS_SINCE: semver::Version = semver::Version::new(2, 1, 286);
+
+/// Whether a CLI of `version` moves running work aside for a person's steer
+/// ([`STEER_MOVES_TOOLS_SINCE`]); an unknown version is treated as not.
+fn steer_moves_tools(version: Option<&semver::Version>) -> bool {
+    version.is_some_and(|version| *version >= STEER_MOVES_TOOLS_SINCE)
+}
+
+/// How a steer goes out ([`wire::SteerPriority`]). On a CLI that moves
+/// running work aside, the person's own steer is `now` as a human message:
+/// the CLI keeps every tool running and the model reads it at once. A
+/// message from another chat is not the person's: it never claims to be
+/// (an interrupt reads as the person rejecting the call), so it, and every
